t, estate administration, endowments, foundations, individual retirement accounts, escrow services, and custody. Further, it offers insurance agency services in the property and casualty area; investment, merger and acquisition advisory services, private debt, equity and mezzanine placement services, and other middle-market advisory services; and other banking services, including telephone and online banking, mobile banking, debit cards, direct deposit and remote deposit capture, mobile deposit option, automated teller machine, and cash management services. Pinnacle Financial Partners, Inc. was incorporated in 2000 and is headquartered in Atlanta, Georgia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Kevin S. Blair | President, CEO & Director | Age 54","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 8K people. Revenue per employee of $240K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $79K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Pinnacle Financial Partners, In is a large-cap financial services business with a $14.0B market cap on $2.1B of annual revenue.","The business throws off $679M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 33 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.18\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA.","Shareholder yield is only 0.4%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev